  "intro": {
    "cards": [
      {
        "title": "The verb changes with the subject",
        "title_cz": "Sloveso podle podmětu",
        "body": "Look at the subject (*podmět*) first. English changes the verb for **one group only**: **he / she / it**.",
        "points": [
          "**She works. They work.**",
          "**She is. They are.** · **She has. They have.**"
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Two groups",
        "title_cz": "Dvě skupiny",
        "body": "Put the subject in its group. Take the form under it. Names and nouns go in too.",
        "points": [
          "**Anna works.** (Anna = she) · **My parents work.** (my parents = they)"
        ],
        "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 520 235\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" font-family=\"Lexend, sans-serif\">\n  <g stroke=\"var(--vocab-accent, #4db6c7)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" fill=\"none\">\n    <rect x=\"20\" y=\"15\" width=\"230\" height=\"130\" rx=\"8\"/>\n    <rect x=\"270\" y=\"15\" width=\"230\" height=\"130\" rx=\"8\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"var(--vocab-accent, #4db6c7)\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n    <text x=\"135\" y=\"44\">he · she · it</text>\n    <text x=\"385\" y=\"44\">I · you · we · they</text>\n  </g>\n  <g font-size=\"22\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"var(--text, #eaeaea)\">\n    <text x=\"52\" y=\"84\" font-size=\"21\">is · has · work<tspan fill=\"#d4b070\">s</tspan></text>\n    <text x=\"281\" y=\"84\" font-size=\"21\">are · have · work</text>\n  </g>\n  <g font-size=\"12\" fill=\"var(--text, #eaeaea)\">\n    <text x=\"90\" y=\"118\">one ending: <tspan fill=\"#d4b070\" font-weight=\"600\">-s</tspan></text>\n    <text x=\"330\" y=\"118\">no -s   ·   I → am</text>\n  </g>\n  <g stroke=\"#d4b070\" stroke-width=\"1.5\">\n    <line x1=\"135\" y1=\"176\" x2=\"135\" y2=\"158\"/>\n    <line x1=\"385\" y1=\"176\" x2=\"385\" y2=\"158\"/>\n  </g>\n  <polygon points=\"130,160 135,150 140,160\" fill=\"#d4b070\"/>\n  <polygon points=\"380,160 385,150 390,160\" fill=\"#d4b070\"/>\n  <g font-size=\"13\" fill=\"var(--text, #eaeaea)\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n    <text x=\"135\" y=\"198\">Anna · my brother · the shop</text>\n    <text x=\"385\" y=\"198\">my parents · Anna and Petr</text>\n  </g>\n  <g font-size=\"12\" fill=\"var(--vocab-accent, #4db6c7)\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n    <text x=\"135\" y=\"220\">= she · he · it</text>\n    <text x=\"385\" y=\"220\">= they</text>\n  </g>\n</svg>"
      },
      {
        "title": "One change only",
        "title_cz": "Jen jedna změna",
        "body": "Czech changes the verb for every person (*pracuju, pracuješ, pracuje, pracujeme…*). English changes it once, for he / she / it. The ending is **-s**, sometimes **-es** (*watches, goes*) — and it is easy to forget.",
        "points": [
          "**He works.** The ending is the only change. Keep it.",
          "**He is. He has.** Same group, its own forms."
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Common mistakes",
        "title_cz": "Časté chyby",
        "body": "Find the subject first. Then the form.",
        "points": [
          "The **-s** is missing: *She work here* → **She works here**",
          "*have* with he / she / it: *He have a car* → **He has a car**",
          "The noun ends in -s and pulls the verb: *My parents works* → **My parents work**"
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
